# The layers whose remainder is claimed to be on or over the line. One row per layer filing
# `interference` or `transition`: demand meets or exceeds supply somewhere in the range.
#
# The side where somebody bears something
#   Under a clearance the supply is above demand everywhere and there is nothing to absorb; here
#   there is, so the holder shares have a magnitude to add up to and the absorbing buffer has a
#   size to fit inside. checks/clearance_with_unserved.sqlc ranges over the complement.
#
# Not the same question as what the buffer absorbed
#   On or over the line is not the same question as "what did the buffer absorb", and both
#   consumers of this relation, entries/borne.sqlc and arithmetic/shares_bounded.sqlc, narrow it
#   again to `interference` for exactly that reason; borne is where the narrowing is argued. Under
#   a `transition` both sides are live at once and no single magnitude here says which one a share
#   is on.
-- pm:Remainder/sign in {interference, transition}.
SELECT r.*
FROM (
    :compose(layers/remainder.sqlc)
) r
WHERE r.sign IN ('interference', 'transition')
